.TH vobsub2srt 2.0.0-rc6 "12 Nov 2026"
.SH NAME
vobsub2srt \- Converts DVD bitmap subtitles (.idx/.sub or directly from a FFmpeg-compatible file) into .srt subtitles using Tesseract OCR and libavcodec et. al.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvobsub2srt\fR [\fIOPTION\fR] \fIFILENAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
vobsub2srt converts subtitles in dvd_subtitle/vobsub (.idx/.sub) format into the .srt format.  VobSub subtitles contain images and srt is a text format.
OCR is used to extract the text from the subtitles.  vobsub2srt uses tesseract for OCR and uses FFmpeg libraries to demultiplex, decode and filter.

Note: VOB files will possibly only work on discs without encryption.


.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fIFILENAME\fR
File name of the subtitles, either the .idx file with or without the file extension, or a container (VOB, MP4, MKV, etc) with DVD subtitles. The .srt subtitles are written to a file called \fIFILENAME.LANG\fR.srt.
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-pgm\fR
Extract the subtitles as NetPBM PGM images (format \fIFILENAME.LANG\fR-\fINUMBER\fR.pgm in PGM format). (Obsolete)
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-png\fR
Extract the subtitles to sequential PNG files.
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR
Print text output to terminal (to stdout).
.TP
\fB\-\-output, \-o\fR
Output subtitles to specified filename.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print verbose information about the subtitle decoding process (to stderr).
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fIlanguage\fR
Select the language of the subtitle (two-letter ISO 639-1 code, e.g. en for English or de for German, or three-letter ISO 639-3 code).
Use \fI--langlist\fR to see the languages in the subtitle file.
.TP
\fB\-\-langlist\fR
List languages and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-index\fR \fIindex\fR
The index of the subtitle to convert.  Use this instead \fI--lang\fR if there are several streams with the same language.
Combining \fI--lang\fR and \fI--index\fR does not work! Usage of \fI--index\fR combined with Tesseract language with \fI--tesseract-lang\fR, e.g. \fI--index 3 --tesseract-lang spa\fR is more reliable.
.TP
\fB\-\-ifo\fR \fIifo-file\fR
To use a specific IFO file for the palette (useful when no OCR happens).
.TP
\fB\-\-tesseract-lang\fR \fIlanguage\fR
Set the language to be used by Tesseract.  This is auto detected in .idx files and normally does not need to be changed.
If however you need special language settings (e.g., deu-frak, chi_sim, chi_tra), or to recognize multiple languages in one set of subtitles, add them together as such: spa+eng.
.TP
\fB\-\-tesseract-data\fR \fIpath\fR
Set path to Tesseract data. (e.g. where your Tesseract \fItraineddata\fR files are, otherwise auto-detect standard Tesseract data).
.TP
\fB\-\-blacklist\fR \fIblacklist\fR
Blacklist characters for OCR (e.g. |\\/`_~<>). Default set to |\/
.TP
\fB\-\-y-threshold\fR \fIthreshold\fR
Y (luminance) threshold below which colors treated as black (Default: 16).
.TP
\fB\-\-min-width\fR \fIwidth\fR
Minimum width in pixels to consider a subpicture for OCR (Default: 8).
.TP
\fB\-\-min-height\fR \fIheight\fR
Minimum height in pixels to consider a subpicture for OCR (Default: 8).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
  $ \fBvobsub2srt foobar.mkvfR; $ \fBvobsub2srt foobar.idx\fR
.fi
Prints the subtitles as they are passed through OCR.\fR
.nf
  $ \fBvobsub2srt \-\-lang en foobar.mkv\fR
.fi
Converts the English language subtitles from the media (VOB, MP4, MKV etc) or VobSub files \fIfoobar.idx\fR/\fIfoobar.sub\fR to srt subtitles in \fIfoobar.srt\fR.
.nf
  $ \fBvobsub2srt \-\-lang zh \-\-tesseract-lang chi_sim foobar\fR
.fi
Converts the chinese language subtitles using simplified chinese (chi_sim) characters.
.nf
  $ \fBvobsub2srt \-\-tesseract-lang deu+eng foobar\fR
.fi
Converts subtitles that have both German and English dialogue in them.
.nf
  $ \fBvobsub2srt \-\-dump-png foobar.mkv\fR
.fi
Extracts individual subtitles to PNG files. Useful to compare to the SRT output.

